1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,240
What is the biggest misconception that you feel people have about the Black future?

2
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:05,420
It's a really important question.

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:10,340
But from my point of view, it's that I think it's wrong to be rooted in hopelessness.

4
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:16,500
I think that when I talk to people like you, when I talk to my peers that I like, I feel like a ton of hope.

5
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:20,780
I know that things can improve maybe more than we could ever believe.

6
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:23,620
So I think hopelessness is kind of a mistake.

7
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:27,380
What's one thing you said in this episode that you would stand 10 toes down on?

8
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:29,460
A ghost story is a realism story.

9
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:30,500
It's all real.

10
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:31,220
It's all true.

11
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:40,420
When you're writing, there could be monsters and dragons and ghosts, or you could be writing about being in a cubicle or waiting in line at the DMV.

12
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,440
Either way, you have to make it real for the reader.

13
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:44,180
So it's all realism to me.

